KMEDIA WASM RUNTIME LICENSE MAP

This repository and the runtime archive are composite works. They are not
licensed as a whole under Apache-2.0 or any other single open-source license.

1. FFmpeg

The complete FFmpeg source archive under `third-party-sources/` and the
FFmpeg portions of the WebAssembly binary are licensed under GNU Lesser
General Public License version 2.1 or later. The exact text is in
`LICENSES/LGPL-2.1.txt`.

2. Relinking scripts and materials

The files under `docker/` that configure, compile, and relink FFmpeg are
provided under LGPL-2.1-or-later so recipients may reproduce and modify the
covered library. The checksum and packaging files may be copied and modified
as necessary to exercise those LGPL rights.

The compiled files under `relink/objects/` contain several components:

- inherited movi-player portions remain under Apache-2.0; see
  `LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt`;
- Signalsmith portions remain under MIT; see
  `LICENSES/Signalsmith-MIT.txt`;
- SuvioMedia-authored portions are all rights reserved except for the express
  object-code permission in `RELINKING_TERMS.md`.

3. dav1d

The prebuilt library and public headers under `relink/dav1d/` are
BSD-2-Clause; see `LICENSES/dav1d-BSD-2-Clause.txt`. Full dav1d source is not
included because its license does not require source publication.

4. Generated runtime components

The loader and WebAssembly binary also contain or derive from Emscripten,
musl, LLVM libc++, and zlib. Their terms are reproduced in:

- `LICENSES/Emscripten.txt`
- `LICENSES/musl.txt`
- `LICENSES/LLVM-libcxx.txt`
- `LICENSES/zlib.txt`

5. Everything else

Unless a file or section above says otherwise, Copyright 2026 KMediaPlayer
contributors. All rights reserved. Public availability does not grant access
to or a license for the private native shim source, Signalsmith integration
source, proprietary Kotlin player, or other product source.

Nothing in this map limits rights granted by a third-party license or by
mandatory law. All materials are provided "as is", without warranty of any
kind, to the maximum extent permitted by law.
